; the workspace of the end-effector in sthira-apeksha (world frame)
; the range of FK: every reachable end-effector position is a point in task-space
; IK maps task-space targets back to joint-space configurations
; for a planar arm: task-space is aayaama-dvaya (2D); for 3D: aayaama-traya

(kosha task-space
  (sthita domain-robotics sthira-apeksha)
  (swarupa akasham bindu)
  (phala kinematic-chain fk)
  (ahara ik)
  (drishthanta aayaama-dvaya aayaama-traya))
